00:56:03,411 --> 00:56:04,976
BECKET: <i>She heard about
the deaths in the family</i>

1198
00:56:05,020 --> 00:56:07,194
<i>and got a laser-based security
system installed</i>

1199
00:56:07,237 --> 00:56:09,281
<i>in all four of her houses.</i>

1200
00:56:09,324 --> 00:56:10,846
<i>But there wasn't
a security system</i>

1201
00:56:10,889 --> 00:56:12,889
<i>at the Blessings
of the Desert Day Spa</i>

1202
00:56:12,933 --> 00:56:15,150
<i>where she spent
every Tuesday afternoon.</i>

1203
00:56:15,194 --> 00:56:16,584
I'm sorry to disturb you.

1204
00:56:16,628 --> 00:56:19,367
We're offering complimentary
teeth whitening services

1205
00:56:19,410 --> 00:56:21,541
until 5 o'clock,
if you're interested.

1206
00:56:22,150 --> 00:56:24,236
I have some literature
on the process,

1207
00:56:24,280 --> 00:56:25,454
safety information,
if you'd like.

1208
00:56:25,497 --> 00:56:26,672
CASSANDRA: I didn't
come here to read.

1209
00:56:30,497 --> 00:56:31,541
Blessings.

1210
00:56:31,975 --> 00:56:35,062
<i>The special ingredient
was carbamide peroxide</i>

1211
00:56:35,454 --> 00:56:36,759
<i>which is so close
to the acidic agent</i>

1212
00:56:36,801 --> 00:56:38,062
<i>found in teeth whitener</i>

1213
00:56:38,106 --> 00:56:39,714
<i>that the police thought
she must have bought</i>

1214
00:56:39,758 --> 00:56:41,584
<i>an off-brand batch
during her last adoption trip</i>

1215
00:56:41,628 --> 00:56:42,845
<i>to Cambodia.</i>

1216
00:56:42,888 --> 00:56:44,497
[CASSANDRA SPEAKING, MUFFLED]
It's tingling.

1217
00:56:45,540 --> 00:56:48,280
- [BELL TOLLS]
- [DUCKS QUACKING]

1218
00:56:48,323 --> 00:56:50,323
[CELL PHONE VIBRATES]

1219
00:56:55,193 --> 00:56:56,671
BECKET: <i>Then there's
my Uncle McArthur.</i>

1220
00:56:56,714 --> 00:56:58,409
Sir, you've got about
a 30-knot wind

1221
00:56:58,453 --> 00:57:00,062
coming out
of the north-northwest.

1222
00:57:00,105 --> 00:57:01,496
- Just so you know.
- Thanks, but I think

1223
00:57:01,540 --> 00:57:03,801
I can handle
some goddamn wind, chief.

1224
00:57:03,845 --> 00:57:05,061
BECKET: <i>This guy owned, like,</i>

1225
00:57:05,105 --> 00:57:06,758
<i>half The National Air
and Space Museum.</i>

1226
00:57:06,801 --> 00:57:08,453
<i>And while the rest of us
were planning</i>

1227
00:57:08,496 --> 00:57:09,931
<i>a long weekend at Key West,</i>

1228
00:57:09,974 --> 00:57:13,583
<i>he was planning an actual
trip to the actual moon.</i>

1229
00:57:14,540 --> 00:57:16,496
JOURNALIST: McArthur,
what do you say to the critics

1230
00:57:16,540 --> 00:57:19,539
who see you spending
$50 million to fly to space

1231
00:57:19,582 --> 00:57:21,495
when half your employees
don't have health insurance?

1232
00:57:21,539 --> 00:57:23,366
Fifty? More like ninety.

1233
00:57:24,322 --> 00:57:27,713
Look, if I could do this kind
of thing for cheap, I would.

1234
00:57:27,757 --> 00:57:29,452
But it's incredibly expensive.

1235
00:57:30,061 --> 00:57:31,452
- Gassed up?
- ASSISTANT: Yes, sir.

1236
00:57:31,495 --> 00:57:32,844
MCARTHUR: Spot check?
ASSISTANT: Yes, sir.

1237
00:57:32,887 --> 00:57:34,191
MCARTHUR: Where's my coffee,
by the way?

1238
00:57:34,234 --> 00:57:35,408
BECKET: Here you go.

1239
00:57:36,844 --> 00:57:38,191
Lock and load.

1240
00:57:38,234 --> 00:57:39,713
BECKET: <i>All it took
was a laminated pass</i>

1241
00:57:39,757 --> 00:57:41,234
<i>and a shirt from the mall.</i>

1242
00:57:41,278 --> 00:57:42,886
[ALARM BLARING]

1243
00:57:44,408 --> 00:57:47,973
MAN: [OVER RADIO] <i>Charlie 17,
you are very low, over.</i>

1244
00:57:48,017 --> 00:57:49,191
[BELL TOLLS]

1245
00:57:49,234 --> 00:57:52,495
1,500 square feet,
three bedrooms, doorman.

1246
00:57:52,538 --> 00:57:54,060
You ever have a doorman before?

1247
00:57:54,843 --> 00:57:56,799
- I barely had a door.
- [REALTOR CHUCKLES]

1248
00:57:56,843 --> 00:57:58,712
REALTOR: It changes your life.
I'm not even joking around.

1249
00:57:59,320 --> 00:58:02,060
This is original marble
from, uh, Italy.

1250
00:58:02,104 --> 00:58:03,320
And if you look out there,

1251
00:58:03,364 --> 00:58:04,886
that's what you pay
the money for.

1252
00:58:12,538 --> 00:58:13,756
So would you want to live here?

1253
00:58:15,103 --> 00:58:16,103
[VEHICLE HONKS]

1254
00:58:16,146 --> 00:58:17,190
With me?

1255
00:58:19,320 --> 00:58:22,929
I know
it's a little fast, but...

1256
00:58:24,494 --> 00:58:26,537
I'd really
like to have you here.

1257
00:58:28,624 --> 00:58:30,146
I'd love it, actually.

1258
00:58:31,493 --> 00:58:32,537
If I'm being honest.

1259
00:58:35,190 --> 00:58:36,232
Uh... [CHUCKLES]

1260
00:58:37,450 --> 00:58:38,493
Um...

1261
00:58:39,972 --> 00:58:41,016
Yeah.

1262
00:58:41,711 --> 00:58:42,711
I'd love that too.

1263
00:58:44,363 --> 00:58:45,668
Now, I know the place is a lot

1264
00:58:45,711 --> 00:58:46,928
but Warren's gonna give me
a bridge loan

1265
00:58:46,971 --> 00:58:48,145
and the neighborhood's
appreciating...

1266
00:58:48,189 --> 00:58:49,319
RUTH: Hey, hey.

1267
00:58:50,363 --> 00:58:52,928
I liked you when you lived
in Newark and took the bus.

1268
00:58:54,319 --> 00:58:55,406
You know that, right?

1269
00:58:58,710 --> 00:58:59,710
What?

1270
00:59:04,579 --> 00:59:05,971
Nothing.

1271
00:59:06,015 --> 00:59:10,971
By the way, I can fire you
at any time, but I won't.

1272
00:59:11,015 --> 00:59:14,231
- [ALL LAUGHING]
- [STAMMERS, CHUCKLES]

1273
00:59:14,275 --> 00:59:17,928
To continue with this story,
and he said, he's, like...

1274
00:59:17,970 --> 00:59:19,318
"What are you talking about?
Where are you?"

1275
00:59:19,362 --> 00:59:20,667
And I was, like,
"I'm in Highland Park."

1276
00:59:21,536 --> 00:59:24,362
He was, like, "No..."

1277
00:59:24,405 --> 00:59:26,709
BECKET: <i>As for the next
Redfellow in line,</i>

1278
00:59:26,753 --> 00:59:28,449
<i>you can probably
guess who it was.</i>

1279
00:59:28,492 --> 00:59:29,927
[WARREN LAUGHS]

1280
00:59:29,970 --> 00:59:31,492
BECKET: <i>But by now,
I couldn't imagine lifting</i>

1281
00:59:31,536 --> 00:59:33,057
<i>a finger against my uncle,</i>

1282
00:59:33,796 --> 00:59:35,578
<i>much less doing the man harm.</i>

1283
00:59:36,448 --> 00:59:39,753
And by that point, things were
going decently well.

1284
00:59:39,796 --> 00:59:42,666
The job, living situation...

1285
00:59:45,361 --> 00:59:46,535
FATHER MORRIS:
You were content.

1286
00:59:49,014 --> 00:59:51,883
Without the wealth.
Without the inheritance.

1287
00:59:55,361 --> 00:59:56,404
Well...

1288
00:59:57,578 --> 00:59:59,317
<i>Maybe you're right.
Maybe I was...</i>

1289
01:00:00,622 --> 01:00:01,665
<i>content.</i>

1290
01:00:02,404 --> 01:00:03,448
<i>Content enough.</i>

1291
01:00:05,839 --> 01:00:07,143
<i>And I suppose I had
more important things</i>

1292
01:00:07,187 --> 01:00:08,361
<i>to think about.</i>

1293
01:00:08,404 --> 01:00:10,274
RUTH: <i>My mom's gonna
want Zinfandel.</i>

1294
01:00:11,187 --> 01:00:13,143
I think we're making
the right choice, by the way.

1295
01:00:13,187 --> 01:00:15,882
Having an engagement party
at your home just feels,

1296
01:00:15,926 --> 01:00:19,229
better than
at a bar or something.

1297
01:00:19,882 --> 01:00:22,055
I totally agree.

1298
01:00:24,795 --> 01:00:26,273
RUTH: I'm still thinking
about your family.

1299
01:00:27,925 --> 01:00:28,968
All the crazy shit.

1300
01:00:29,968 --> 01:00:30,968
Okay.

1301
01:00:32,012 --> 01:00:33,099
I don't mean to obsess,

1302
01:00:33,142 --> 01:00:35,273
but don't you think that it's...

1303
01:00:35,316 --> 01:00:37,229
BECKET: I'm not even
a part of that family.

1304
01:00:37,881 --> 01:00:39,447
Whatever's going on, it's got
nothing to do with us.

1305
01:00:40,751 --> 01:00:42,273
Besides, it's probably
over anyway.

1306
01:00:43,489 --> 01:00:44,489
RUTH: What makes you say that?

1307
01:00:48,142 --> 01:00:49,142
I don't know.

1308
01:00:49,664 --> 01:00:50,707
Just sayin' it.

1309
01:00:51,707 --> 01:00:53,664
- [TRAFFIC BUSTLING]
- [DISTANT SIRENS BLARING]

1310
01:00:58,576 --> 01:01:01,098
PINFIELD: Excuse me.
Mr. Redfellow?

1311
01:01:01,141 --> 01:01:02,359
Becket Redfellow?

1312
01:01:05,141 --> 01:01:06,141
How you doing today?

1313
01:01:09,837 --> 01:01:10,880
[BECKET CLEARS THROAT]

1314
01:01:13,750 --> 01:01:14,837
MATTHEWS: Nice office
you got here.

1315
01:01:16,750 --> 01:01:18,750
I like it. [CHUCKLES]

1316
01:01:18,793 --> 01:01:19,837
PINFIELD:
Just so we understand,

1317
01:01:19,880 --> 01:01:21,141
you said you're not an heir

1318
01:01:21,185 --> 01:01:22,227
to the estate, is that correct?

1319
01:01:23,098 --> 01:01:24,098
As far as I know.

1320
01:01:24,837 --> 01:01:27,314
Well, we did
a little research, and...

1321
01:01:28,227 --> 01:01:29,271
Congratulations.

1322
01:01:41,792 --> 01:01:42,792
BECKET: Wow.

1323
01:01:43,401 --> 01:01:45,618
Uh, it's just a little...

1324
01:01:46,271 --> 01:01:47,531
I... I had no idea.

1325
01:01:48,184 --> 01:01:50,792
Hmm. Can you answer
a few questions for us?

1326
01:01:50,836 --> 01:01:52,010
Yeah, I'm... I'm sorry.

1327
01:01:52,053 --> 01:01:53,574
Um, I... I really had no idea.
This is...

1328
01:01:53,618 --> 01:01:54,792
PINFIELD: Nobody's
arguing with you.

1329
01:01:56,705 --> 01:01:57,879
MATTHEWS: Can you tell us
where you were

1330
01:01:57,923 --> 01:01:59,053
on the afternoon of April 10th?

1331
01:01:59,097 --> 01:02:00,487
It would've been a Sunday.

1332
01:02:04,487 --> 01:02:05,531
BECKET: Oh...

1333
01:02:06,487 --> 01:02:08,444
April 10th. Okay. Here we go.

1334
01:02:08,965 --> 01:02:10,052
MATTHEWS: You're
fucking kidding me.

1335
01:02:11,357 --> 01:02:13,313
He remembers when
and where he bought a hot dog.

1336
01:02:13,835 --> 01:02:14,878
Is that even him?

1337
01:02:15,357 --> 01:02:16,400
I don't know.

1338
01:02:16,878 --> 01:02:17,878
Can you see who it is?

1339
01:02:20,183 --> 01:02:22,052
PINFIELD: I can't see shit.
MATTHEWS: Me neither.

1340
01:02:22,096 --> 01:02:23,791
PINFIELD: All right,
follow him.

1341
01:02:23,835 --> 01:02:27,009
WOMAN: Rothburn's going down,
and Bellman's gonna go too.

1342
01:02:27,052 --> 01:02:28,748
They're minutes away,
I guarantee it.

1343
01:02:28,791 --> 01:02:30,573
MAN: I say we dump
whatever we can cut loose

1344
01:02:30,617 --> 01:02:32,096
before the markets catch wind.

1345
01:02:32,138 --> 01:02:34,704
WOMAN: We can say we were
forced into it, which is true.

1346
01:02:35,399 --> 01:02:36,443
No.

1347
01:02:38,269 --> 01:02:39,617
I spent 35 years

1348
01:02:39,661 --> 01:02:41,661
earning the trust
of these shareholders.

1349
01:02:42,964 --> 01:02:44,312
I'm not throwing them
to the sharks

1350
01:02:44,356 --> 01:02:45,573
in one afternoon.

1351
01:02:45,617 --> 01:02:47,661
[CELLPHONE RINGING]

1352
01:02:49,964 --> 01:02:52,312
- Oh, shit.
- BECKET: What?

1353
01:02:52,356 --> 01:02:53,660
[WARREN EXHALES DEEPLY]

1354
01:02:57,921 --> 01:03:00,398
- Goddamn! [GRUNTING]
- Oh, whoa. Oh, oh, oh!

1355
01:03:03,355 --> 01:03:05,008
- [GASPING]
- MAN: Is he all right?

1356
01:03:07,181 --> 01:03:08,572
- Becket...
- Call an ambulance!

1357
01:03:13,572 --> 01:03:15,442
WARREN: <i>Pass me that water,
will ya?</i>

1358
01:03:16,442 --> 01:03:18,485
[GRUNTS, GULPING]

1359
01:03:22,442 --> 01:03:24,311
[EXHALES, SIGHS]

1360
01:03:26,181 --> 01:03:27,224
[CHUCKLES]

1361
01:03:27,920 --> 01:03:29,833
Listen, I'm not
gonna mince words.

1362
01:03:33,224 --> 01:03:35,267
You want to chase that rabbit
down the hole, huh?

1363
01:03:36,571 --> 01:03:38,571
Okay. That money rabbit.

1364
01:03:40,050 --> 01:03:41,484
Everybody loves a good chase.

1365
01:03:44,615 --> 01:03:45,659
And you're good at it.

1366
01:03:47,919 --> 01:03:49,093
But here I am,

1367
01:03:50,136 --> 01:03:51,615
61 years old and...

1368
01:03:54,267 --> 01:03:56,441
you're the only visitor
I've had all day.

1369
01:04:00,832 --> 01:04:03,006
Go find that person
in your life, Becket.

1370
01:04:05,614 --> 01:04:06,658
Whoever it is.

1371
01:04:08,353 --> 01:04:09,527
Work at loving them.

1372
01:04:12,006 --> 01:04:13,570
I mean, really work.

1373
01:04:16,006 --> 01:04:17,048
'Cause...

1374
01:04:17,875 --> 01:04:18,961
at the end of the day...

1375
01:04:20,701 --> 01:04:22,179
it's the only job that pays.

1376
01:04:29,092 --> 01:04:31,135
[DUCKS QUACKING]

1377
01:04:31,179 --> 01:04:32,961
[CHORAL MUSIC PLAYING]

1378
01:04:39,526 --> 01:04:41,005
BECKET: <i>It was in this
unhappy moment</i>

1379
01:04:41,048 --> 01:04:43,135
<i>that I realized an ironic truth.</i>

1380
01:04:45,048 --> 01:04:46,395
<i>There is only one left.</i>

1381
01:04:47,961 --> 01:04:49,482
MAN: You can either
get rid of it,

1382
01:04:49,526 --> 01:04:51,047
or do what you like.

1383
01:04:53,960 --> 01:04:55,221
But not here.

1384
01:04:57,221 --> 01:04:58,526
Not under this roof.

1385
01:05:02,830 --> 01:05:05,178
And I think you know
I have to stand by that.

1386
01:05:07,656 --> 01:05:09,091
A man of my word.

1387
01:05:10,221 --> 01:05:12,394
BECKET: <i>One left.</i>

1388
01:05:13,612 --> 01:05:15,221
<i>But what use was it
to fantasize?</i>

1389
01:05:15,264 --> 01:05:17,699
<i>I had put all that behind me.</i>

1390
01:05:17,743 --> 01:05:20,047
Hey, Becket. Letter for you.

1391
01:05:20,960 --> 01:05:21,960
- Thanks, Brian.
- Yep.

1392
01:05:30,177 --> 01:05:31,656
[CHORAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

1393
01:05:35,742 --> 01:05:37,220
- [MUSIC STOPS]
- [CELL PHONE VIBRATING]

1394
01:05:38,655 --> 01:05:40,394
- Hey.
- He invited me.

1395
01:05:40,438 --> 01:05:41,480
RUTH: [OVER PHONE] <i>What?</i>

1396
01:05:42,177 --> 01:05:43,220
My grandfather.

1397
01:05:44,307 --> 01:05:46,785
To a dinner party
at the estate. [CHUCKLES]

1398
01:05:48,133 --> 01:05:50,219
- <i>Hello?</i>
- Uh, I just...

1399
01:05:50,263 --> 01:05:52,785
I... I thought you said
you would never do that?

1400
01:05:52,829 --> 01:05:54,176
- Never do what?
- RUTH: <i>Never meet the guy.</i>

1401
01:05:54,219 --> 01:05:55,567
<i>Wait, when is this?</i>

1402
01:05:55,611 --> 01:05:57,524
- Tonight.
- <i>It's Friday.</i>

1403
01:05:57,567 --> 01:05:59,176
- BECKET: I know.
- Friday.

1404
01:05:59,742 --> 01:06:01,306
BECKET: <i>Oh, shit.</i>

1405
01:06:01,350 --> 01:06:04,655
Ruth, I may not have
this opportunity again.

1406
01:06:04,698 --> 01:06:06,306
He never sees anyone.

1407
01:06:06,350 --> 01:06:08,437
RUTH: <i>You may not have
this opportunity again?</i>

1408
01:06:08,480 --> 01:06:10,045
- I don't know.
- <i>Yeah, you're right.</i>

1409
01:06:10,089 --> 01:06:11,828
So be home by 7:00
or you will miss

1410
01:06:11,871 --> 01:06:14,393
your own fucking engagement
party, like... [SCOFFS]

1411
01:06:14,437 --> 01:06:16,610
Right. Of course. Of course.

1412
01:06:17,915 --> 01:06:18,915
Okay.

1413
01:06:19,392 --> 01:06:20,871
I love you, by the way.

1414
01:06:25,262 --> 01:06:26,262
I'm gonna call you back.

1415
01:06:28,697 --> 01:06:30,349
Package for Mr. Redfellow.

1416
01:06:44,262 --> 01:06:45,349
Remember to breathe.

1417
01:06:46,305 --> 01:06:47,392
Very important.

1418
01:06:48,870 --> 01:06:50,522
[CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKS]

1419
01:06:52,783 --> 01:06:54,088
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

1420
01:06:56,565 --> 01:06:57,653
Taylor drowned.

1421
01:06:59,174 --> 01:07:00,914
He went to Princeton
on a swimming scholarship

1422
01:07:00,957 --> 01:07:02,348
and he drowned.

1423
01:07:03,870 --> 01:07:06,043
I became more than a bit
suspicious right then.

1424
01:07:07,174 --> 01:07:09,043
So I had a little friend
follow you.

1425
01:07:10,348 --> 01:07:11,696
Aren't those great?

1426
01:07:13,391 --> 01:07:14,782
I'm really happy
I went with black and white.

1427
01:07:16,739 --> 01:07:18,348
[SIGHS DEEPLY]

1428
01:07:21,174 --> 01:07:22,391
[GRUNTS, SLAMS TABLE]

1429
01:07:24,608 --> 01:07:25,652
BECKET: What do you want?

1430
01:07:28,174 --> 01:07:29,434
Finish it.

1431
01:07:31,521 --> 01:07:33,434
I'm under investigation
by the FBI.

1432
01:07:33,477 --> 01:07:34,913
And yet here you are.

1433
01:07:36,086 --> 01:07:37,303
It's almost as if, I don't know,

1434
01:07:37,347 --> 01:07:38,477
they don't quite have a case.

1435
01:07:40,129 --> 01:07:41,739
Which is bananas.

1436
