<i>And being rich</i>

1686
01:24:56,142 --> 01:24:58,403
<i>is even better than you imagine.</i>

1687
01:24:59,533 --> 01:25:01,229
[MUSIC CONCLUDES]

1688
01:25:04,576 --> 01:25:07,316
[CLOCK TICKING]

1689
01:25:08,837 --> 01:25:11,358
You know I mentioned earlier,
this is a tragedy.

1690
01:25:13,707 --> 01:25:14,707
Still is.

1691
01:25:16,098 --> 01:25:18,315
Donald Macnamara, my wife.

1692
01:25:18,358 --> 01:25:19,532
- Such a pleasure.
- Nice to meet you.

1693
01:25:19,576 --> 01:25:20,750
Nice to meet you.

1694
01:25:21,402 --> 01:25:24,141
- RUTH: Hi.
- Nancy Dillard, the Dillards.

1695
01:25:24,620 --> 01:25:25,923
- Nice to meet you.
- NANCY: Mmm-hmm.

1696
01:25:26,880 --> 01:25:27,880
Megan Pinfield.

1697
01:25:27,923 --> 01:25:29,097
FBI.

1698
01:25:30,010 --> 01:25:31,141
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

1699
01:25:32,315 --> 01:25:33,358
Hello.

1700
01:25:37,531 --> 01:25:39,358
Can you shut that door
behind you, please?

1701
01:25:41,010 --> 01:25:42,010
[BECKET SIGHS]

1702
01:25:45,401 --> 01:25:49,183
Look, not to be uncouth,
but this is...

1703
01:25:49,227 --> 01:25:50,270
heroically bad timing.

1704
01:25:50,314 --> 01:25:51,793
Yeah, you're under arrest.

1705
01:25:51,836 --> 01:25:53,401
I need you to stay calm
and cooperate.

1706
01:25:53,444 --> 01:25:56,575
- I'm under arrest? For what?
- For murder.

1707
01:25:59,009 --> 01:26:00,140
Of who?

1708
01:26:01,444 --> 01:26:02,792
Lyle Archdale.

1709
01:26:04,401 --> 01:26:06,705
[CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING]

1710
01:26:12,183 --> 01:26:13,227
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

1711
01:26:16,748 --> 01:26:18,183
RUTH: Hey, wait!

1712
01:26:20,183 --> 01:26:21,835
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

1713
01:26:23,400 --> 01:26:24,661
RUTH: What do we do?

1714
01:26:25,313 --> 01:26:26,356
What do we do?

1715
01:26:27,095 --> 01:26:28,530
[ENGINE ROARING]

1716
01:26:29,313 --> 01:26:30,661
Ruth, I love...

1717
01:26:32,530 --> 01:26:34,748
[MUSIC CONTINUES]

1718
01:26:48,747 --> 01:26:50,095
BECKET: <i>Can you believe it?</i>

1719
01:26:51,226 --> 01:26:52,704
<i>After all this,</i>

1720
01:26:52,747 --> 01:26:54,921
<i>I'd go down for a killing
I didn't even commit.</i>

1721
01:26:54,965 --> 01:26:56,312
NEWS REPORTER: <i>Now we wanna
point out to listeners</i>

1722
01:26:56,355 --> 01:26:58,921
<i>that Becket Redfellow
crossed state lines,</i>

1723
01:26:58,965 --> 01:27:01,704
<i>which is why his trial
is unfolding in federal court</i>

1724
01:27:01,747 --> 01:27:04,181
<i>where murder can still mean
capital punishment</i>

1725
01:27:04,225 --> 01:27:05,834
<i>for citizens of New Jersey.</i>

1726
01:27:06,704 --> 01:27:09,225
As we can see
from these security tapes,

1727
01:27:10,138 --> 01:27:11,964
Mr. Redfellow
burst into the office

1728
01:27:12,007 --> 01:27:14,138
at approximately 5:03 p.m.,

1729
01:27:14,616 --> 01:27:16,920
and then emerged
just four minutes later,

1730
01:27:17,703 --> 01:27:19,442
which is consistent
with the estimated time

1731
01:27:19,485 --> 01:27:21,094
of Mr. Archdale's death.

1732
01:27:22,268 --> 01:27:24,354
Now, we've heard
from the coroner

1733
01:27:25,051 --> 01:27:26,790
that he estimates
the time of death

1734
01:27:26,833 --> 01:27:29,224
between 5:06 and 5:15 p.m.

1735
01:27:29,790 --> 01:27:30,877
And we've heard

1736
01:27:30,920 --> 01:27:32,659
from the eyewitness
in the hallway,

1737
01:27:32,703 --> 01:27:35,180
who positively identifies
Mr. Redfellow.

1738
01:27:36,180 --> 01:27:38,137
Sir, can you confirm that
this is the murder weapon?

1739
01:27:38,790 --> 01:27:40,963
Uh, I can confirm
that it is, yes.

1740
01:27:41,006 --> 01:27:42,224
And did you find
the defendant's fingerprints

1741
01:27:42,267 --> 01:27:43,354
on the murder weapon?

1742
01:27:43,398 --> 01:27:44,919
FORENSICS EXPERT:
I did, yes.

1743
01:27:44,963 --> 01:27:47,528
How certain are you that, uh,
these are his fingerprints?

1744
01:27:47,572 --> 01:27:48,658
FORENSICS EXPERT:
I'm 100% certain.

1745
01:27:48,702 --> 01:27:49,745
BECKET: <i>A letter opener.</i>

1746
01:27:53,093 --> 01:27:56,093
My entire life
because of a letter opener.

1747
01:27:56,137 --> 01:27:58,963
PROSECUTOR: You were the first
to find your husband's body.

1748
01:27:59,484 --> 01:28:00,789
Is that correct?

1749
01:28:00,832 --> 01:28:01,876
Yes.

1750
01:28:02,658 --> 01:28:06,484
Tell me. Were you in love with
Mr. Redfellow at the time?

1751
01:28:06,527 --> 01:28:07,615
[JULIA SNIFFLES]

1752
01:28:08,615 --> 01:28:10,310
Yes. [CRYING]

1753
01:28:10,353 --> 01:28:12,049
PROSECUTOR:
And he with you?

1754
01:28:18,179 --> 01:28:20,527
Becket Redfellow
has been in love with me

1755
01:28:21,310 --> 01:28:23,614
his entire life. [SNIFFLES]

1756
01:28:24,223 --> 01:28:25,744
[JULIA SOBBING]

1757
01:28:25,788 --> 01:28:28,439
I just never thought he would
do something like this.

1758
01:28:28,483 --> 01:28:30,614
[SOBBING]

1759
01:28:31,744 --> 01:28:32,918
I'm sorry.

1760
01:28:34,265 --> 01:28:35,701
JUDGE: <i>Will the defense
please rise?</i>

1761
01:28:37,875 --> 01:28:39,222
Upon the verdict,

1762
01:28:39,265 --> 01:28:41,875
the jury finds the defendant,
Becket Redfellow,

1763
01:28:41,918 --> 01:28:44,309
guilty of murder
in the first degree

1764
01:28:44,352 --> 01:28:45,657
as charged in the indictment

1765
01:28:45,701 --> 01:28:47,091
and that the punishment of death

1766
01:28:47,135 --> 01:28:48,483
- shall be imposed.
- [INDISTINCT CONVERSATION]

1767
01:28:48,526 --> 01:28:50,396
JUDGE: May the sentence
be recorded by the clerk.

1768
01:28:50,439 --> 01:28:52,222
May God rest his soul.

1769
01:28:52,265 --> 01:28:53,526
Thank you.

1770
01:28:53,570 --> 01:28:54,830
[GAVEL BANGS]

1771
01:28:56,439 --> 01:28:58,352
BECKET: <i>I wish I could find
the right words</i>

1772
01:28:58,396 --> 01:29:00,352
<i>to describe this juncture
in my story.</i>

1773
01:29:02,004 --> 01:29:03,613
[DOOR BUZZING]

1774
01:29:04,135 --> 01:29:05,308
[DOOR SLAMS]

1775
01:29:05,351 --> 01:29:07,525
PRISON GUARD: Cell 15, secure!

1776
01:29:11,482 --> 01:29:13,482
BECKET: <i>But there are
no right words.</i>

1777
01:29:15,743 --> 01:29:16,787
[EXHALES]

1778
01:29:16,830 --> 01:29:18,090
<i>There's only time.</i>

1779
01:29:20,351 --> 01:29:22,221
<i>- And silence.</i>
- [CLOCK TICKING]

1780
01:29:24,221 --> 01:29:26,264
[CLOCK TICKING]

1781
01:29:31,482 --> 01:29:33,568
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

1782
01:29:38,699 --> 01:29:39,742
[FOOTSTEPS HALT]

1783
01:29:40,350 --> 01:29:41,481
- PRISON GUARD: Yo.
- [THUMPING ON RAILS]

1784
01:29:41,524 --> 01:29:43,394
You got a visitor.

1785
01:29:53,263 --> 01:29:54,828
PRISON GUARD:
You got three minutes.

1786
01:29:56,176 --> 01:29:57,220
[BECKET SIGHS]

1787
01:30:10,828 --> 01:30:11,828
[INHALES]

1788
01:30:14,349 --> 01:30:16,654
You must be quite the catch
back there.

1789
01:30:22,698 --> 01:30:24,393
You got a big day
coming up, huh?

1790
01:30:27,219 --> 01:30:29,436
You remember that game
we used to play as kids?

1791
01:30:30,740 --> 01:30:32,262
I'd have a secret, and...

1792
01:30:33,436 --> 01:30:34,567
you'd try to guess what it was.

1793
01:30:34,610 --> 01:30:35,958
If you've got
something to say, say it.

1794
01:30:38,610 --> 01:30:40,306
All right.
I'll give you a hint.

1795
01:30:41,653 --> 01:30:43,784
- It involves handwriting.
- You're foul.

1796
01:30:46,045 --> 01:30:48,566
You're a lump of coal
with makeup.

1797
01:30:50,871 --> 01:30:52,914
I'd rather die in here
than be with you.

1798
01:30:55,958 --> 01:30:57,348
I'll give you another hint.

1799
01:30:57,392 --> 01:30:58,610
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

1800
01:30:59,957 --> 01:31:01,000
Lyle...

1801
01:31:02,697 --> 01:31:04,392
when I found him like that...

1802
01:31:06,087 --> 01:31:08,044
I found something else, too.

1803
01:31:09,000 --> 01:31:10,522
And beautifully written,
I might add.

1804
01:31:11,174 --> 01:31:12,348
What's with the white?

1805
01:31:12,392 --> 01:31:13,957
Are you boys playing doctor
back there?

1806
01:31:14,000 --> 01:31:15,521
Did Lyle leave a note?

1807
01:31:15,565 --> 01:31:17,870
Is that what you're saying?
Did Lyle leave a note?

1808
01:31:19,609 --> 01:31:21,131
- JULIA: You know...
- If Lyle wrote a note...

1809
01:31:21,174 --> 01:31:23,217
- I think I might just leave...
- If that's what you're saying,

1810
01:31:23,260 --> 01:31:25,434
in the name of all things holy,
you have to release it.

1811
01:31:27,434 --> 01:31:29,260
- Oh, now you want to talk?
- What do you want?

1812
01:31:29,304 --> 01:31:30,956
[BREATHING SHAKILY]

1813
01:31:30,999 --> 01:31:32,521
- What do you want?
- Becket...

1814
01:31:33,521 --> 01:31:35,609
What could you possibly have
to offer?

1815
01:31:36,825 --> 01:31:39,478
No, no, no, no, no!
Hey, hey, hey! Stop!

1816
01:31:39,521 --> 01:31:41,782
- That's it! [GRUNTING]
- Tell me! Stop! Stop!

1817
01:31:41,825 --> 01:31:43,260
I have 30 seconds!

1818
01:31:43,304 --> 01:31:44,782
- PRISON GUARD: You got 25.
- Okay.

1819
01:31:44,825 --> 01:31:46,738
- Sit down.
- Julia!

1820
01:31:47,391 --> 01:31:49,304
Julia, come here, please!
Please!

1821
01:31:49,347 --> 01:31:50,825
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

1822
01:31:53,999 --> 01:31:55,043
Okay.

1823
01:32:00,129 --> 01:32:01,129
What do you want?

1824
01:32:06,477 --> 01:32:08,042
- Just give me a moment.
- [SLAMS FIST]

1825
01:32:10,564 --> 01:32:12,346
I'm gonna die in 24 hours.

1826
01:32:13,216 --> 01:32:14,607
You don't want that to happen.

1827
01:32:14,650 --> 01:32:16,520
I know you don't want that
to happen.

1828
01:32:18,129 --> 01:32:20,172
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

1829
01:32:23,911 --> 01:32:25,085
Give me everything.

1830
01:32:28,345 --> 01:32:30,129
- Sign it over to...
- [LINE DISCONNECTS]

1831
01:32:43,389 --> 01:32:45,084
[ALARM BUZZING]

1832
01:32:45,128 --> 01:32:46,389
[THUDS]

1833
01:32:50,823 --> 01:32:52,345
[EXHALES]

1834
01:32:59,041 --> 01:33:00,693
PRISON GUARD:
You need anything else?

1835
01:33:02,562 --> 01:33:03,954
Got a priest?

1836
01:33:06,606 --> 01:33:08,388
Well, that was some hours ago.

1837
01:33:09,867 --> 01:33:10,996
And if you're curious

1838
01:33:11,040 --> 01:33:14,866
why I've been so calm
and self-assured

1839
01:33:14,909 --> 01:33:16,909
for a man
set to be executed in...

1840
01:33:20,562 --> 01:33:24,561
it's because I thought
our friend Julia, might, uh...

1841
01:33:27,214 --> 01:33:29,561
might come through in the end.

1842
01:33:30,822 --> 01:33:31,909
[INHALES]

1843
01:33:36,779 --> 01:33:37,953
I wonder if she's coming.

1844
01:33:49,082 --> 01:33:50,605
FATHER MORRIS:
"The Lord is my shepherd

1845
01:33:51,169 --> 01:33:52,430
"I shall not want.

1846
01:33:53,691 --> 01:33:56,169
"He maketh me to lie down
in green pastures.

1847
01:33:57,430 --> 01:33:59,865
"He leadeth me
beside the still waters."

1848
01:33:59,908 --> 01:34:01,213
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

1849
01:34:01,256 --> 01:34:02,995
"He restoreth my soul.

1850
01:34:03,995 --> 01:34:05,865
"He leadeth me
in the paths of righteousness

1851
01:34:05,908 --> 01:34:07,255
"for his name's sake.

1852
01:34:08,342 --> 01:34:09,473
"Yea, though I walk through

1853
01:34:09,516 --> 01:34:10,865
"the valley
of the shadow of death

1854
01:34:10,908 --> 01:34:12,604
"I will fear no evil

1855
01:34:13,342 --> 01:34:14,604
"for thou art with me.

1856
01:34:15,994 --> 01:34:18,604
"Thy rod and thy staff
they comfort me."

1857
01:34:18,647 --> 01:34:19,864
[CLOCK TICKING]

1858
01:34:19,907 --> 01:34:23,516
[FATHER MORRIS CONTINUES
INDISTINCTLY]

1859
01:34:25,820 --> 01:34:26,994
PRISON GUARD: Redfellow.

1860
01:34:28,777 --> 01:34:30,603
You're not gonna
fuckin' believe this.

1861
01:34:32,255 --> 01:34:34,125
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

1862
01:34:34,168 --> 01:34:35,472
POLICE CHIEF:
First and foremost,

1863
01:34:35,515 --> 01:34:38,212
we have absolute faith
in our forensic team...

1864
01:34:38,255 --> 01:34:41,733
[CONTINUES INDISTINCTLY]

1865
01:34:48,385 --> 01:34:49,515
PRISON GUARD: <i>Open 15.</i>

1866
01:34:50,124 --> 01:34:51,690
[DOOR SLIDING OPEN]

1867
01:34:51,733 --> 01:34:52,733
Let's go.

1868
01:34:55,776 --> 01:34:57,950
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

1869
01:35:01,689 --> 01:35:02,732
[RUSTLING]

1870
01:35:03,515 --> 01:35:05,602
[DOOR BUZZING]

1871
01:35:19,602 --> 01:35:20,776
[SIGHS SOFTLY]

1872
01:35:33,688 --> 01:35:34,731
[SIGHS]

1873
01:35:35,384 --> 01:35:36,427
BECKET: You came.

1874
01:35:48,166 --> 01:35:49,688
[CAR DOOR CLOSES,
ENGINE STARTS]

1875
01:35:51,688 --> 01:35:53,165
[TIRES SCREECHING]

1876
01:35:53,209 --> 01:35:54,644
[ENGINE ACCELERATING]

1877
01:36:09,904 --> 01:36:11,339
[SIGHS HEAVILY]

1878
01:36:23,817 --> 01:36:24,904
[LATIN POP MUSIC PLAYING]

1879
01:36:24,948 --> 01:36:25,948
[SIGHS]

1880
01:36:33,251 --> 01:36:34,295
[SIGHS]

1881
01:36:37,816 --> 01:36:38,816
All right.

1882
01:36:55,990 --> 01:36:57,990
